id:                     E474
trigger_tool: HAP|ArkUI|native-consumer|management-observer
phase: target-consumer-validation|result-reconciliation
error_signature: native consumer stages are present but an auxiliary snapshot or management acknowledgement is missing; a loose validator changes the four-consumer result
severity: 2
category: consumer-observer-separation
match_keywords: API20 snapshot acknowledgement, observer timeout, nativewindow, OHAudio, consumers_total, NOT_REQUIRED, NOT_RUN, authoritative terminal receipt
title: Separate auxiliary observers from the native consumer terminal contract
root_cause: A surface snapshot and a management acknowledgement are observation or transaction-control contracts, while core, invalid-input, audio, and video are product consumers. Treating an observer as a fifth consumer, or accepting locally printed stage fields without an authoritative terminal receipt, makes a missing observer look like a consumer failure or a consumer success.
affected_scope: API-level UI test hosts, multimedia or graphics adapters, and any target runner that combines native capability checks with an optional screenshot or external management channel.
verification_cmd: Run the host contract with four ordered consumer stages; require an explicit snapshot policy; inspect the authoritative terminal schema and reject a count derived from an observer timeout; retain upstream and target denominators separately.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: typed-consumer-and-observer-receipts
rec_description: Define the exact consumer set and denominator first. Emit each stage only after the production native operation, record optional observers as NOT_REQUIRED or NOT_RUN, and accept consumers_passed/consumers_total only from a terminal receipt bound to the same run identity and input snapshot.
rec_command: validate source contract; compile and run a host fixture; verify ordered core_pass invalid_pass audio_pass video_pass markers; assert snapshot=NOT_REQUIRED or a separate required receipt; preserve upstream=0/0 NOT_RUN for a consumer-only run
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fail-closed-reconciliation
fallback_description: If observer policy or terminal authority is unavailable, leave the run nonterminal and keep the consumer count unproven; do not promote local output or historical upstream evidence.
fallback_command: read only the existing receipts and classify NOT_RUN or FAIL; create a new run identity for any code repair
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: snapshot.*fifth.*consumer|observer.*timeout.*consumers_passed|version.*smoke.*native.backend
forbid_1_reason: A screenshot or control-channel event does not exercise the native video or audio path and cannot alter the declared consumer denominator.
forbid_1_consequence: False failures, false passes, and an unreviewable test denominator.
forbid_2_pattern: local.*stage.*fields.*terminal.*PASS|history.*upstream.*consumer-only
forbid_2_reason: Stage text without a bound terminal receipt and historical upstream runs belong to different evidence scopes.
forbid_2_consequence: An incomplete target transaction can be reported as a completed current run.
